WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.000
Water.

2
00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:02.330
Bread and wine.

3
00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:03.270
Oil.

4
00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.790
Christians use all of them in worship.

5
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:10.640
The Church of England's Book of Common Prayer
has a famous definition of a sacrament.

6
00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:15.330
An outward and visible sign of
an inward and spiritual grace.

7
00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:20.570
Yet in 1883, The Salvation Army
stopped celebrating the sacraments.

8
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.520
So why do some Christians
count seven sacraments,

9
00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:26.370
some two, and some none at all?

10
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.290
In this mission, you'll
see what a sacrament is,

11
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:32.050
and how the Catholic Church
groups seven of them.

12
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.470
Then you'll place each
Christian tradition on one bar.

13
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.200
Your mission: explain why Christians
disagree about how many sacraments there

14
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:40.670
are.
